      <Ordine>30</Ordine>
      <Capitolo>Automatic transmission oil level check</Capitolo>
      <Corpo> &lt;html xmlns:v=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml&quot; xmlns:o=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; xmlns:w=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word&quot; xmlns:m=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2004/12/omml&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40&quot;&gt;     &lt;body lang=IT style=&apos;tab-interval:35.4pt&apos;&gt;  &lt;div class=WordSection1&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;font-size:12.0pt; line-height:107%;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; The gearbox must not be in recovery mode&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Make sure that the temperature of the gearbox oil is not higher than &lt;B&gt;30 °C.&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Should the temperature be higher, it is recommended to allow the gearbox oil to cool down.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Place the vehicle on a level&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Place the shift lever in &lt;B&gt;P&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Make sure the parking brake is engaged&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Connect the tubes of the suction instrument &lt;B&gt;VAS 6622A&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Start the engine at idle&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Ensure that the air conditioning and heating system are turned off.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Connect the diagnostic tester and wait for vehicle identification&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Via diagnostic tester start the automatic transmission oil level check procedure&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Remove the bottom cover&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Place the oil extractor pan &lt;B&gt;VAS 6622A &lt;/B&gt;under the gearbox.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Remove the drain plug &lt;B&gt;A&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Allow the accumulated transmission oil to escape from the overflow pipe &lt;B&gt;B&lt;/B&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CAUTION:&lt;/B&gt;There are different versions of the overflow pipe.&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CAUTION:&lt;/B&gt;Damage to the gearbox can occur if overfilling or underfilling occurs&lt;B&gt;.&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Make sure that the overflow tube is mounted correctly&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CHANGE WITH BEIGE OVERFLOW TUBE: &lt;/B&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; - The oil level must not exceed the mouth of the overflow tube &lt;B&gt;B &lt;/B&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; - For checking and exact adjustment of the oil level, it is necessary to give &lt;B&gt;2 turns &lt;/B&gt;to unscrew the overflow tube&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;GEARBOX WITH RED OVERFLOW TUBE:&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; It is not necessary to unscrew the red overflow tube to check the oil level&lt;B&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;span style=&apos;mso-spacerun:yes&apos;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;CONTINUATION FOR ALL VEHICLES:&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; If the gearbox oil temperature is between &lt;B&gt;35~45°C &lt;/B&gt;and some oil comes out (due to temperature rise), the oil level is regular.&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt;A small amount of transmission oil leaks out of the overflow tube &lt;B&gt;B &lt;/B&gt;every 30 seconds due to coolant pulses. This spillage is irrelevant to the oil level check.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal style=&apos;margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt&apos;&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Do not reuse gearbox oil that has already spilled again&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; If necessary, top up the gearbox oil with new oil&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; If the oil level is regular, screw in the overflow tube &lt;B&gt;B &lt;/B&gt;if necessary and tighten it to &lt;B&gt;3 Nm&lt;/B&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;#61623; Tighten the drain plug &lt;B&gt;A &lt;/B&gt;to &lt;B&gt;45 Nm.&lt;/B&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt;Always replace the gasket of the drain plug &lt;B&gt;A&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;/body&gt;  &lt;/html&gt;</Corpo>
